            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CV Therapeutics, under license from Roche (formerly Syntex), is developing ranolazine (Ranexa), a metabolic modulator and a partial fatty acid oxidation inhibitor, for the potential treatment of angina and acute coronary syndromes. By October 2004, enrollment in the phase III MERLIN TIMI-36 study was ongoing and the company anticipated completion by the end of the first quarter of 2005.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
